# APP01-07: Ubuntu and Nextcloud Security Hardening

## Objective

The objective of this task was to improve the security, performance, and operational resilience of the APP01 Nextcloud server by applying production-recommended hardening measures. The implementation focused on PHP optimisation, memory caching, transactional file locking, additional PHP modules, and system maintenance to prepare the server for secure deployment.

---

## 1. Configure PHP Memory Limit

### Purpose

Nextcloud recommends a minimum PHP memory limit of 512 MB to ensure reliable application performance during large file uploads, background jobs, application updates, and administrative operations.

### Implementation

The Apache PHP configuration was updated from 128 MB to 512 MB.

The PHP CLI configuration remained unchanged with an unlimited memory allocation to support administrative OCC commands.

### Verification

The Apache PHP configuration was verified after restarting the Apache service.

The PHP memory warning was successfully removed from the Nextcloud Administration Overview page.

---

## 2. Install APCu Memory Cache

### Purpose

APCu provides local in-memory caching for frequently accessed PHP objects. This reduces database queries, improves response time, and lowers server resource consumption.

### Implementation

The APCu PHP module was installed and enabled.

Nextcloud was configured to use APCu as the local memory cache.

The PHP CLI configuration was updated to enable APCu for OCC commands.

### Verification

The APCu module was successfully detected by PHP.

The APCu warning was removed from the Nextcloud Administration Overview page.

---

## 3. Configure Redis Transactional File Locking

### Purpose

Redis provides transactional file locking to prevent simultaneous file access conflicts and improve data integrity during concurrent user operations.

### Implementation

Redis Server and the PHP Redis extension were installed.

Redis was enabled as a system service.

Nextcloud was configured to use Redis for transactional file locking.

### Verification

The Redis service was verified as active.

The Nextcloud configuration confirmed:

- memcache.local = APCu
- memcache.locking = Redis

The transactional file locking warning was successfully removed.

---

## 4. Install Additional PHP Components

### Purpose

Additional PHP and ImageMagick components improve compatibility and performance while satisfying Nextcloud production recommendations.

### Implementation

ImageMagick SVG support was installed.

The Apache service was restarted after installation.

### Verification

The ImageMagick warning disappeared from the Nextcloud Administration Overview page.

---

## 5. Run MIME Type Migration

### Purpose

MIME type migration updates existing file associations to support newer file types and improve compatibility.

### Implementation

The Nextcloud maintenance repair command was executed with expensive repair tasks enabled.

### Verification

The MIME migration warning was successfully removed.

---

